{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/384862-quality-guardian-rant","id":384862,"title":"'Quality Guardian' Rant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-29T02:02:09-08:00","id":384862,"title":"'Quality Guardian' Rant","content":"Just looking to let off some steam about something that bugs me. If you have something constructive to say, I'm happy to hear it, and I'll do my best to take it on board. But please don't try to convince me I'm wrong; I may well be, but I do not much care.<br /> <br /> I've had quite enough of this anti-Twilight, anti-Friday, anti-popular thing that seems to be everywhere. It's not new, I'm sure, but it drives me up the wall how people pick something seemingly arbitrarily, and declare it the &quot;Worst X EVAR&quot;. Twilight, particularly, seems victim of this. Now, I'm not a fan of the books; I find them dull, characters one-dimensional at best, and I'm not entirely sure if it has a plot. But that's really irrelevant outside of my own head and decisions. Lots of people like them, and hey, good for them, they found something that makes their lives a bit brighter. I know I could use a bit more of that. But no. &quot;We can't have that!&quot; say the Quality Guardians. &quot;People must only like what we <i>say</i> they can like! Game of Thrones* for all!&quot; So they bitch and moan, insulting everyone who <i>dares</i> have a different opinion than them. Anne Rice took more liberties with the vampire mythos than Meyer, nobody's calling her work unforgivably crap and insulting people who like them. Or at least it's happening a lot less and I don't have to deal with it. So everywhere I turn, if the <i>word</i> 'twilight' is mentioned, regardless of context, you're looking at minimum of 20 minutes bagging on the series and movies, with implicit or explicit calling of anyone who disagrees with them mentally retarded or totally lacking in taste. Because it's totally impossible to have different opinions and not have one party be stupid, right? So when my father thinks my fondness for fantasy novels is silly and boring, and I find military books overblown and stupid, who's stupid? Come on, break out your magic qualitometre, I've got a sippy cup to give and voting rights to withdraw!<br /> <br /> What's really annoying is that, by a lot of measurements, Twilight <i>is</i> good. Do I like it? No. But a <i>lot</i> of people do, it's hugely influential, massively successful, and it is actually kind of innovative in its own little way. Vampires sparkling sounds silly, but so did vampires being burned by sunlight back in the 1920s or whenever Nosferatu was made. Certainly wasn't a part of Dracula, and hardly universal in the mythos predating it. And hell, at least it dealt with the thirst; Underworld didn't even do that in any significant fashion, and that did really well as a movie. Given that quality is, for the most part, entirely subjective, those are as reasonable metrics to apply as any other. Nobody was saying superheroes were good literature back in the 30s and 40s, yet look at the impact they've had up to now. Same with the noir detective thing, psychedelic movies and arty innovations of the 60s, and hell, even The Matrix. Do I like them? No, not really. But they were successful, had a huge impact, and a lot of people did, and they've stood the test of time and are still relevant today.<br /> <br /> It also happens with music. Now, nobody is seriously claiming Rebecca Blacks &quot;Friday&quot; is the next big thing in music. Her career is pretty much non-existent, and her song wasn't that good. Wasn't even really meant for distribution. But oh no, someone is trying, can't have that! Let's send her death threats and threaten to rape her and utterly devalue her as a person because she sang a substandard song that she didn't even write! I don't care if she was 14 at the time, I know <i>I've </i>never done anything silly at 14, and everyone who does grows up to be a horrible, horrible human being who strangles puppies and burns orphans! After all, every time someone likes or makes a bad song (because that can be determined empirically with 100% reliability and validity, after all), the Earth moves a little closer to the sun, speeding our mass extinction.<br /> <br /> I thought we'd come to the conclusion a while back that quality was largely subjective? You know, that whole &quot;beauty is in the eye of the beholder/one mans trash is another mans treasure&quot; thing we went to all the trouble to come up with proverbs for?<br /> <br /> We see plenty of discussion about inclusiveness and acceptance in our hobby, and maybe that's a discussion that needs to happen. I haven't seen these issues in actual play myself, but I'm willing to accept that they're out there. But you can't say &quot;we need to be inclusive of people, regardless of their sexuality/race/gender/favourite Pringle flavour&quot; and then turn around and belittle people because they like a different book series than you. Screw worrying about whether Prince is a misogynistic term, how about we focus on the little stuff? If we start accepting things that are totally subjective and opinion-based, maybe it'll be easier to accept things about people that they can't change.<br /> <br /> But of course we all know that the works themselves have nothing to do with this. It's just people trying to make themselves feel better by banging on someone elses efforts. &quot;I can't write my name, but at least I didn't write Twilight!&quot; &quot;I suck at guitar because I can't be arsed practising, but at least I'm a better musician than Rebecca Black!&quot; &quot;Why would I try to be a more moral person, I'm better than Mel Gibson and his anti-Semetic rants!&quot; Bashing people is just way easier than doing better, and accepting that other people have a differing opinion requires <i>so much work</i>. Gotta quiet those nagging voices of inadequacy somehow, after all.<br /> <br /> So, while I can understand the appeal to bitch and moan to make yourself feel better, please don't fall into the trap of appointing yourself Quality Guardians. Someone likes something that you don't, that's fine. You can disagree, even discuss why. I know a lot of people don't really like Evanescence, but I thoroughly enjoy most of their music. That's my right. And it's your right to disagree. But it is <i>not </i>your right to attack people for having differing opinions.<br /> <br /> You know. Unless you're God. Then I suspect you have more important things to be doing, and hopefully aren't so petty as to worry about people seeing a silly vampire romance film. And if you are, then I think you have deeper issues you might want to look at.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">*</span> Chose Game of Thrones because I don't see the appeal and it's popular. You like it, good for you. It's an example, go with it.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T04:48:47-08:00","id":384906,"title":"","content":"I have the feeling I mostly agree with the gist of your rant, but that you didn't choose the best examples. Twilight, for example, from everything I understand about it secondhand, is not good, but not because supernatural teenage romance with vampires who sparkle like diamonds in the sun is intrinsically bad. Rather, because there's a lot of creepy codependence going on in it that Stephanie Meyer didn't intend to convey. (Even then, I have to add the caveat that I haven't read the books or seen the movies. Just because supernatural romance isn't a bad thing doesn't mean it's my personal thing.) That said, I'm pretty sure a lot of the people expressing reflexive resistance to the idea of shiny vampires don't really know much more about Twilight than that.<br /> <br /> Friday is hilariously bad, but you're right that a lot of people misplace the blame for it. Rebecca Black isn't the perpetrator of some offense against taste, she's the victim of some skeevy music producers who misrepresent themselves to teen girls and their parents with pie-in-the-sky dreams and bleed them dry for vanity projects with slapdash writing and direction. She deserves sympathy; the exploitative, lazy dude who wrote the song does not, and has gone on to pretty much continue to do the exact same thing. I hadn't heard that she'd received death or rape threats, but I absolutely would believe it.<br /> <br /> <i>Edit:</i> At a second glance and catching some bits I hadn't noticed, I'd also be <i>very</i> careful about contrasting this idea with issues of inclusivity. People feeling left out because society excludes them and erases their identity as a person, and people feeling left out because they like a book or a show that the subculture turns its nose up at, are two very different issues, and if you think the latter is a more pressing issue, I think you ought to consider if you're venting enough heat that you're saying things without thinking, or otherwise, reconsider your priorities. Besides, it's a false dilemma, and one that's often used to devalue arguments toward inclusivity, to imply that only one of these issues can be worked on at a given time. There's not a single well of nonrenewable social justice that has to be rationed carefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 01-29-2015, 07:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T05:00:20-08:00","id":384911,"title":"","content":"I agree, the problem I have with Twilight (if I have any at all) is all the romanticazing (?) of very wrong things regarding relationships (all the stalking, verbal abuse and derision and the complete dependency and dehumanization). That's bad and the fact that it got consummed and asimilated by a lot of young (and not so young) girls is horrible in and of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T05:05:21-08:00","id":384913,"title":"","content":"Is 'Friday' any worse than anything, say, Megan Trainor has put out? Or Jason Derulo? Or, hell, most pop stars? Yeah, it's shallow, repetitive, and massively over-autotuned, but there's at least 10 songs on the Hot 100 at any given time that those criticisms can be levelled at just as easily. It's dump pop, really: just noise, but pleasant enough noise, easily ignorable. But yes, you're right: if there has to be blame, which I am not convinced of, then it rests on the writers and producers: it <i>is</i> their job to sell this stuff, after all. And yeah, she mentioned in an interview I think that she's gotten a lot of threats, to the point where her family was seriously considering hiring a bodyguard.<br /> <br /> And we can go back and forth on what Meyer intended; unless she actively says, we'll never really know. And it's not really important anyway. I'm sure people read all sorts of things into the media I enjoy; god knows roleplaying hasn't been exactly criticism-free from that angle. Hell, I liked the Infernals splat; disgusting as it was, it was appropriate given the context (they <i>are</i> in Hell, after all. Not meant to be nice), and maybe the writers intended all that stuff, maybe they didn't. The Lunar splat has certainly got a disjoint between intent and how it reads, and I like that too. But nobody would seriously entertain the idea of censoring me for my opinion on that, or accuse me of being mentally retarded. So why is it OK to do it based on teenage girls liking a book aimed at teenage girls? Frankly, if you wanted to get upset about that, I'd get upset about the lack of quality writing aimed at that demographic, but that's not something you can really blame any individual work on.<br /> <br /> As to your inclusivity point, you're right... sort of. Is it the same thing? No, of course not, the sheer scale alone differentiates them. But when you're around a gaming table, people insulting your gender/race/sexual orientation and people insulting your taste in media, while one may or may not be more upsetting (depends on the individual, I suspect), they're both insulting. So by focussing on one, which is affected by millions of factors and mostly is the result of social and cultural factors, while the other is, in theory at least, more easily addressed? Sexism/racism/etc is complex. Saying &quot;Everyone who likes X is stupid&quot; is more simple, and is easier to address, and <i>might</i> help create that more inclusive feeling people are going for. Might not, who knows. Won't fix the other problems, obviously, but I doubt it'd hurt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 01-29-2015, 08:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T05:07:36-08:00","id":384915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/384862-quality-guardian-rant?p=384911#post384911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, the problem I have with Twilight (if I have any at all) is all the romanticazing (?) of very wrong things regarding relationships (all the stalking, verbal abuse and derision and the complete dependency and dehumanization). That's bad and the fact that it got consummed and asimilated by a lot of young (and not so young) girls is horrible in and of itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is it horrible? Is a demographic you don't belong to (I assume?) consuming media you don't enjoy a precursor to the End Times? Pop crap has been around since Gutenberg, really, or at least since the means of distribution existed, and I'd say our species has done OK despite that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T05:29:53-08:00","id":384916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/384862-quality-guardian-rant?p=384913#post384913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But yes, you're right: if there has to be blame, which I am not convinced of, then it rests on the writers and producers: it <i>is</i> their job to sell this stuff, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The blame rests on them because they misrepresented their job, in this sense: Rebecca Black and her family assumed it was their job to sell this stuff <i>to the public,</i> but what they actually intended to do was sell the song <i>to the Black family.</i> The Black family paid Ark Music Factory four thousand dollars to produce the video, and they retained ownership over both the master and the intellectual property. All the profit made from people buying the song on iTunes or whatever for a lark? Ark Music pocketed that, not Rebecca Black. Now, Rebecca Black was neither their first nor last client; most of the clients they seek out pay thousands of dollars and end up with a video nobody ever even notices exists.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T05:41:47-08:00","id":384919,"title":"","content":"Entirely legitimate points. I suspect, however, the people bitching are not really upset about the ethical violations vis a vie music royalties","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T06:00:41-08:00","id":384929,"title":"","content":"You are so missing my point is not even funny anymore. Young girls are going to internallize that that kind of pathological jealousy and control is what love and relationships are about. Its already happening, actually, with a great peak on abusive behaviour as part of teenage relationships as of late. That's sad and horrible. I don't much care about the quality of the books/films, it's a problem of very bad and toxic ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T08:02:55-08:00","id":385034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/384862-quality-guardian-rant?p=384915#post384915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it horrible? Is a demographic you don't belong to (I assume?) consuming media you don't enjoy a precursor to the End Times? Pop crap has been around since Gutenberg, really, or at least since the means of distribution existed, and I'd say our species has done OK despite that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Please read again what Thorbes actually wrote about how his problem is with the stalking, codependance and abuse in the relationships depicted in the book. <br /> <br /> In your reply you are basically saying abusive relationship is OK...which I seriously doubt it was your intention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T10:06:35-08:00","id":385234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/384862-quality-guardian-rant?p=384915#post384915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is it horrible?</div> </div> </div> </div>I kind of feel like he answered that in his post.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/384862-quality-guardian-rant?p=384915#post384915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is a demographic you don't belong to (I assume?) consuming media you don't enjoy a precursor to the End Times?</div> </div> </div> </div>I admit I have a tendency to skim, but even so, I'm pretty sure Thorbes did not say that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/384862-quality-guardian-rant?p=384915#post384915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pop crap has been around since Gutenberg, really, or at least since the means of distribution existed, and I'd say our species has done OK despite that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, humanity is okay. That doesn't make a specific toxic idea less toxic, though. It just means that if you insist the only standard of judgment is of the human species as a whole, the damage done to any one group is probably pretty insignificant.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T10:20:21-08:00","id":385241,"title":"","content":"If the core of your message is &quot;Don't be this guy: &quot;<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tU2aqt_BUV0\" data-code=\"tU2aqt_BUV0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tU2aqt_BUV0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div> ...then I agree. However, I reserve the right to not like Twilight myself, and to form first impressions of other people by their taste in media (i.e. if I don't like what you like, and you don't like what I like... is there enough common ground for friendship?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":908,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","user":"semicasual","date":".  CLARIFICATION!!!! 01-29-2015, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T10:44:52-08:00","id":385283,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>semicasual</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/384862-quality-guardian-rant?p=385241#post385241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the core of your message is &quot;Don't be this guy: &quot;<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=tU2aqt_BUV0\" data-code=\"tU2aqt_BUV0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/tU2aqt_BUV0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div></div> </div> </div> ...then I agree. However, I reserve the right to not like Twilight myself, <b>and to judge the character of other people by their taste in media </b>(i.e. if I don't like what you like, and you don't like what I like... is there enough common ground for friendship?)</div> </div> </div> </div> Ok, I agree with you about not liking what other people like but one of my oldest friends who I do trust, loves a lot of things that I consider horrid (4th edition D&amp;D is one example...there are more) but a like for one thing or even a few things does not mean I should judge them. If it is a large swath of things that they enjoy, I can get behind your sentiment of &quot;I doubt we could be friends&quot; but do not look at someone because they like something that you do not like and go &quot;Yeah, you are a shitty person.&quot;<br /> I love things that others make fun of (wrestling is one example that I am teased about with most of my friends) but not a single one of them look down on me about it. Instead, they just make a joke and then I pick something of theirs and make a passing joke and we move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T11:18:34-08:00","id":385305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>thedonnie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/384862-quality-guardian-rant?p=385283#post385283\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I agree with you about not liking what other people like but one of my oldest friends who I do trust, loves a lot of things that I consider horrid (4th edition D&amp;D is one example...there are more) but a like for one thing or even a few things does not mean I should judge them. If it is a large swath of things that they enjoy, I can get behind your sentiment of &quot;I doubt we could be friends&quot; but do not look at someone because they like something that you do not like and go &quot;Yeah, you are a shitty person.&quot;<br /> I love things that others make fun of (wrestling is one example that I am teased about with most of my friends) but not a single one of them look down on me about it. Instead, they just make a joke and then I pick something of theirs and make a passing joke and we move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sometimes the differences in taste aren't so wide that you can't bridge the gap. Sometimes they are.<br /> <br /> Either way, I'm mostly talking about first impressions, which are almost always pretty shallow. If you don't know anything else about a person except that they like something you despise, I don't think that it's unreasonable to conclude that they're mentally very different from you and that you don't want to spend time with them. That doesn't mean you should belittle them or shun them, just that you recognize how dissimilarity creates a gap between you both and you may not have common interests.<br /> <br /> If you've known somebody for years and suddenly find they're into a genre of whatever you don't like, feel free to blow it off. Presumably you've got more to share than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the frontier of the Wild South, there's only one woman with the grit to take on its most dangerous outlaws and bring them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/984977-back-alive-or-maybe-dead-quest\" target=\"_blank\">Back Alive, or Maybe Dead.</a><br /> <br /> Avatar by <a href=\"http://puzzlinghappenstance.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">K.S. Brenowitz</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/908-semicasual","name":"semicasual","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar908_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T13:49:32-08:00","id":385522,"title":"","content":"I read the entire first post and I totally agree with your point. He'll there are genres in the wod I can't stand but I'd never rage on their respective forums. And I've been the target of a few of my friends since my Fandom doesn't expand to game of thrones or dr. Who.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-29T17:00:52-08:00","id":385664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/384862-quality-guardian-rant#post384862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just looking to let off some steam about something that bugs me.<u> If you have something constructive to say, I'm happy to hear it, and I'll do my best to take it on board. But please don't try to convince me I'm wrong; I may well be, but I do not much care.</u></div> </div> </div> </div>See, I put this part in there for a damn <i>reason</i>. But no, we can't possibly have someone questioning the mass hatred we have for our designated target! &quot;Twilight is terrible and forces people to become abusive vampires!&quot; And rock music makes people rebellious, rap makes people violent, and roleplaying is a recruitment tool for Satanists.<br /> <br /> Cause, you know, free will isn't a thing, and only <i>you</i> have the mental capacity to differentiate reality from not-reality. Cause you're <i>special</i>. Everyone else in the world just blindly follows the media they portray.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","user":"Allan53","date":". 01-29-2015, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T03:32:27-08:00","id":386114,"title":"","content":"Ok, I thought the thread was about not making shallow critics based on percieved quality (or lack thereof) of media. I don't think I can be any more clear on this: I don't have any problem about the quality of that fiction. I don't have an irrational hate on for vampires that sparkle because as far as I am concerned is just the nth twist in one of the less consistent parts of the myth and folklore (ie. how the sun affects them).<br /> <br /> I COMPLETELY AGREE WITH YOUR ORIGINAL POST.<br /> <br /> Has that became clear enough?<br /> <br /> What I am against is selling pathological behaviour as completely sane.<br /> <br /> I am not the only one capable of differentiating between reality and fiction, I don't think I'm so special, thank you.<br /> <br /> That said, is naive at best and dangerously ignorant at worst to beliebe everyone at any age has the same capacity to do so. It is ignorant in the extreme to deny that we are a social animals that learn by imitation in the first stages of development. It is also imposible to ignore that teenagers are at a crossroads where the role models they seek out (or are fed, because media manipulates all of us to varied degrees) will inform how they will act as adults.<br /> <br /> Is Twilight the ultimate source of abusive behaviour? No, it's not, I'm not crazy.<br /> <br /> Is Twilight an example of very bad role models targeted at a particularly maleable age group? Yes, yes it is.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying Twilight is bad quality fiction. I don't even care about giving my opinion on that, that's not the point. It is chock full of very toxic ideas that should not have had that traction and wide distribution.<br /> <br /> That's it. You can call me a brainless hater for not wanting my little sister to grow up thinking her boyfriend looking through her last phone calls is the ultimate expression of love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T05:44:42-08:00","id":386235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/384862-quality-guardian-rant?p=385664#post385664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, I put this part in there for a damn <i>reason</i>. But no, we can't possibly have someone questioning the mass hatred we have for our designated target!</div> </div> </div> </div>At the risk of sounding more harsh than I intend to--which, for the record, is &quot;not at all,&quot; because I got nothing against you, Allan53--I think if you want to start a conversation and dictate that the only people who are allowed to respond are people who agree with you, then a public discussion forum is the wrong place to do so. You might try a blog or Facebook or something that gives you the authority to mediate comments. As it stands...well, I genuinely am sorry if this comes off as an attack, but you simply do not have standing here to demand that the only opinion allowed to be expressed is your own and those that echo it. Trust me, I've tried it, and it didn't work out for me either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/384862-quality-guardian-rant?p=385664#post385664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cause, you know, free will isn't a thing, and only <i>you</i> have the mental capacity to differentiate reality from not-reality. Cause you're <i>special</i>. Everyone else in the world just blindly follows the media they portray.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well this just seems uncalled-for. Are you feeling okay, Allan53?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/271-jimb","name":"JimB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar271_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T06:46:56-08:00","id":386297,"title":"","content":"This is particularly jarring because I was the first to like the OP, as I was completely on board with the idea. I sincerely don't know what is happening anymore. I think we are talking past each other for some reason.<br /> <br /> Allan53, despite what JimB said, which is true, you still have the option of Flaging any post you think may constitute threadcrapping, as that is agaisnt the terms of use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-30T18:47:46-08:00","id":386929,"title":"","content":"Frankly, no, I'm not feeling OK. I'm intensely angry nearly all the time, no matter what I do. I try to remain calm, and let people be, but their sheer stupidity and egocentricity and arrogance just drives me up the wall. It doesn't help that they accuse me of being arrogant when I have the temerity to talk authoritatively about areas where I either am working on advanced degrees (psychology) or have been making quite a reasonable amount of money for years (economics/company finance). I know, anger isn't helpful, and for years I did my best to control it, but more and more people around me are intent on making their problems my problem, and on the rare occasions I've been stupid enough to ask for their help (ask for their help, not just scream at them and blame them for my insecurities), they universally do not help. Oh, they'll <i>say</i> they will, but good luck getting them to follow through without constant nagging. And maybe it's me, but I don't think you should have to nag your friends to get them to do what they said they would? Remind, sometimes, sure. I forget stuff too. No. This is nagging.<br /> <br /> Now, the odds of me only meeting toolbags is rare, I know, and maybe it's me. But I've tried again and again to approach things properly, or at least the best I can do, and it doesn't seem to help. They're still making everything someone elses problem. You're upset that your job didn't renew your contract for as long as you'd like? Oh, poor baby, at least you've <i>got</i> a job, which is better than me (I'm good at what I do, but it's in the nature of shares that it's inconsistent, which makes bills hard to plan for). But god forbid I point out that their situation isn't so bad, otherwise I get screamed at for being inconsiderate. And if I try to be sympathetic, we all need to just vent sometimes, then god help me if I put one foot wrong, because otherwise it's back to being screamed at. So, while it <i>might</i> be my fault, at least partially, it seems increasingly unlikely. Or at least the standards are insane, to the point where I don't think it's possible.<br /> <br /> And if I try to vent, then I get people jumping all over me because their opinion is so freaking important. I say I don't like a particular political party? I'm inundated with things saying that that political party is actually fantastic and flawless and totally always right, and the one I usually support (even though I've been quite clear that I disagree with a lot of their decisions lately) is literally modern-day Nazis (note: in that case, do not point out that you are Jewish and you had family literally flee the actual Nazis, and thus don't enjoy the comparisons. It won't change what they say, just extend it by an hour). And god forbid you like something unpopular, or dislike something popular.<br /> <br /> So, yeah. I'm pissed off. And I wanted to vent about something that annoyed me in a safe place without being jumped all over. I'm tired of having to walk on eggshells around people because they can't be fucked regulating their emotions, and being attacked if I'm even a little bit out of line, which is more or less inevitable because the lines make no sense and change without warning - not that they acknowledge the changing, you're just being deliberately hurtful.<br /> <br /> Is this bad? Yeah, probably. What, exactly, am I supposed to do about it? Because at this point, I'm inclined towards people just being way more trouble than they're worth. I can deal with them as participants, mostly because that context is really specific and structured, and it's almost always only one interaction. But socially? Not so much. I game for <i>fun</i>, and to hang out with cool people. But if they're going to make it so hard, then why should I bother?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}